{
 "format": "estate-crucible-horror/1",
 "id": "H-0052",
 "title": "Copybook version drift: one member in three libraries with three layouts; SYSLIB order (per program) picks the layout",
 "category": "copy",
 "issue": 4265,
 "collision": true,
 "shapes": [
  "ORDREC in ORDRCPY (41 bytes), SHRCPY (35 bytes) and the retired ORDROLD (36 bytes)",
  "ORDR's SYSLIB is ORDRCPY, ORDRDCL, SHRCPY, ORDROLD; ORDVOLD's own is ORDROLD, ORDRCPY, SHRCPY",
  "SHIP has no ORDREC of its own: its COPY ORDREC takes SHRCPY's",
  "TAXR's ADDRREC shadows SHRCPY's ADDRREC (a longer postal code)"
 ],
 "asserts": "Each COPY resolves to the first library in its program's SYSLIB order that holds the member, and the record's layout is that member's. Every unqualified COPY whose member sits in more than one library of that order is a collision the scan should report, with the winner and the shadowed libraries (key channel copy_collisions; the libraries and orders are key/manifest.json copy_libraries).",
 "citations": [
  {
   "doc": "Enterprise COBOL for z/OS 6.4 Language Reference (SC27-8713-03)",
   "section": "Copy member search order (p.697)",
   "url": "https://publibfp.dhe.ibm.com/epubs/pdf/igy6lr40.pdf",
   "quote": "If no library name is specified in the COPY statement, the concatenation of datasets allocated to the SYSLIB ddname is searched."
  },
  {
   "doc": "z/OS V2R2 DFSMS Using Data Sets (SC23-6855-03)",
   "section": "Concatenating PDSs",
   "url": "https://publibz.boulder.ibm.com/epubs/pdf/dgt3d410.pdf",
   "quote": "If two members of different data sets in the concatenation have the same name, the FIND macro determines the address of the first one in the concatenation."
  }
 ],
